WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.079
This is AIOS:

00:00:02.079 --> 00:00:04.736
my personal AI operating system.

00:00:05.036 --> 00:00:09.050
It turns several AI models into one team that works on my projects,

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:10.846
remembers what it has learned,

00:00:10.846 --> 00:00:13.422
and asks before it does anything important.

00:00:14.872 --> 00:00:17.965
Most AI tools start every conversation from zero,

00:00:17.965 --> 00:00:19.227
in their own window,

00:00:19.227 --> 00:00:20.552
with their own rules.

00:00:20.852 --> 00:00:24.163
I wanted one system where the models share context,

00:00:24.163 --> 00:00:25.591
follow the same rules,

00:00:25.591 --> 00:00:27.278
and stay under my control.

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:30.659
AIOS is built in layers.

00:00:30.959 --> 00:00:33.343
At the top is a desktop control panel.

00:00:33.643 --> 00:00:38.196
Under it runs ClaudeOS, powered by Claude Code, which owns the system.

00:00:38.196 --> 00:00:42.423
Codex joins as an expert partner for reviews and second opinions.

00:00:42.723 --> 00:00:44.841
Routine work goes to fast workers:

00:00:44.841 --> 00:00:48.764
Groq in the cloud, and Ollama models running locally on my Mac.

00:00:50.214 --> 00:00:53.654
Inside ClaudeOS, named agents have clear roles.

00:00:53.954 --> 00:00:55.733
MoMo coordinates the work.

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:59.033
CoCo builds, and runs engineering loops.

00:00:59.333 --> 00:01:01.049
FiFi does the research.

00:01:01.349 --> 00:01:03.698
A Groq research agent searches the web,

00:01:03.698 --> 00:01:07.553
and local Ollama models handle private or bulk tasks at no cost.

00:01:09.003 --> 00:01:10.986
Memory lives in the Second Brain:

00:01:10.986 --> 00:01:15.252
a shared folder of plain files that every agent reads before it starts.

00:01:15.552 --> 00:01:19.500
Hot memory holds current tasks, messages and decisions.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.811
Each project keeps its own memory and handoff notes,

00:01:22.811 --> 00:01:25.242
and older knowledge moves to cold storage.

00:01:25.542 --> 00:01:29.145
It is all versioned in git, so every change can be traced.

00:01:30.595 --> 00:01:32.003
Rules come first.

00:01:32.303 --> 00:01:36.312
A shared contract and a list of prohibited actions apply to every agent.

00:01:36.612 --> 00:01:37.590
Anything risky,

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:38.764
like merging code,

00:01:38.764 --> 00:01:40.917
pushing to git or deleting files,

00:01:40.917 --> 00:01:43.591
becomes a proposal in the approval inbox,

00:01:43.591 --> 00:01:45.091
in English and Finnish,

00:01:45.091 --> 00:01:46.787
and waits for my decision.

00:01:48.237 --> 00:01:51.363
A scheduler built on Node-RED runs tasks on its own.

00:01:51.663 --> 00:01:52.907
Nightly maintenance,

00:01:52.907 --> 00:01:56.139
a memory organiser that keeps the Second Brain tidy,

00:01:56.139 --> 00:01:57.321
and research loops.

00:01:57.621 --> 00:02:01.096
Every run writes a log, and failures show up as alerts.

00:02:02.546 --> 00:02:05.133
The control panel is an Electron desktop app.

00:02:05.433 --> 00:02:08.606
A live graph shows the Second Brain and how it connects.

00:02:08.906 --> 00:02:11.265
Charts track usage for each provider,

00:02:11.565 --> 00:02:17.211
and from one chat box I can talk to any agent, run a task, or approve an inbox item.

00:02:18.661 --> 00:02:20.016
Away from the desk,

00:02:20.016 --> 00:02:24.224
AIOS Remote lets me ask for status or file a note by voice,

00:02:24.224 --> 00:02:25.294
from my iPhone.

00:02:26.744 --> 00:02:28.181
One team of models.

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:29.543
One shared memory.

00:02:29.543 --> 00:02:30.450
Clear rules.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.155
That's AIOS.
